    "aboutAppTitle": "About the app",
    "aboutAppIntro": "A short guide to how each part of ShelfShare works. Open a section for details.",
    "aboutAppXpTitle": "XP and levels",
    "aboutAppTrustTitle": "Trust Score",
    "aboutAppTrustBody": "The Trust Score is a number between 0 and 100 calculated from your actual activity: verified email, how many exchanges you completed successfully, how fast you reply to messages, how old the account is, reviews received. It's not an identity check - it's an indicator that helps others know if you're a trustworthy swap partner. The more you interact and the better you do it, the higher it goes.",
    "aboutAppShelvesTitle": "My Shelf (Public Bookshelf)",
    "aboutAppShelvesBody": "The Shelf is your personal reading status for a book, regardless of whether you own a physical copy or not.\n\n• Reading — the book you're working on now\n• Want to read — your wishlist for the future\n• Read — books you've finished\n\nBooks you can swap or sell are separate - they sit in „My Library\" (My Shelf in the menu). A book can be both on the shelf (ex. „Want to read\") and in the library (ex. „I have a copy to sell\") - these are two different concepts.",
    "aboutAppHomeSectionsTitle": "The 3 sections on Home",
    "aboutAppHomeSectionsBody": "Home is the feed with the latest listings. Between rows you'll see 3 themed sections:\n\n• Most Sought After — the most viewed books on the platform\n• Close near you (100 km) — books within that radius from your city. Hidden if you have no city set or nothing nearby\n• Recommended for you — books filtered by the genres and authors in your profile. If you haven't filled the reader survey, the section doesn't appear",
    "aboutAppExchangesTitle": "Exchanges and offers",
    "aboutAppExchangesBody": "Two ways to get a book from someone else:\n\n• Exchange — you propose a book from your library in exchange for one from another user's library. It's free, only shipping cost\n• Price offer — if a book is listed for sale and marked „negotiable\", you can send an offer with a different price. The seller accepts, rejects or counter-offers",
    "aboutAppBadgesTitle": "Badges (Achievements)",
    "aboutAppBadgesBody": "Badges are awarded automatically when you reach certain milestones: first swap, 10 swaps, 50 swaps, first review written, first member of the community, supporter badge (if you back the project through „Keep the app alive\"), etc.\n\nThey're visible on your public profile. They don't have any functional impact - they just recognize the contribution.",
    "aboutAppChatTitle": "Chat",
    "aboutAppChatBody": "You can start a conversation directly from a book's page or another user's profile. All messages are encrypted in transit.\n\nSimple safety rule: never share personal data (ID number, card number, full address) in chat. For exchanges, use your postal address only when you're sure of the partner.",
    "aboutAppAccountDeletionTitle": "Account deletion",
    "aboutAppAccountDeletionBody": "If you want to delete your account, you can do it from Settings → „Delete account\". After confirmation you have a 15-day grace period during which you can change your mind (log back in and hit „Cancel deletion\"). After 15 days, the account and all data tied to it are permanently deleted.",
    "aboutAppSustainabilityTitle": "Sustainability",
    "aboutAppSustainabilityBody": "Every book swap is one less new book that has to be printed, shipped, and packaged. Buying a new copy costs paper, water, and energy - a copy that already exists, finding a new reader, skips all of that.\n\nShelfShare is part of a growing European movement toward a circular economy: reusing instead of constantly producing new things. A book swap is a small act, but it counts.",
