    "chatSafetyHeadline": "Welcome to Chat",
    "chatSafetyIntro": "This is where you talk to other readers about swaps, offers and books. Pick a conversation from the left, or keep a few rules in mind before you start.",
    "chatSafetyPersonalTitle": "Don't share personal data",
    "chatSafetyPersonalBody": "ID number, card number, home address or passwords — never in chat. Not even if „it's needed for delivery\" or if someone insists.",
    "chatSafetyPaymentTitle": "Safe payments",
    "chatSafetyPaymentBody": "For sales, use protected methods (bank transfer with invoice, cash on delivery). Avoid up-front payments to users with no history.",
    "chatSafetyMeetupTitle": "Meet in a public place",
    "chatSafetyMeetupBody": "For in-person swaps, pick a café, a library or a central square. Don't invite someone to your home on a first swap.",
    "chatSafetyReportTitle": "Report anything suspicious",
    "chatSafetyReportBody": "A user asking for personal data, insisting on unusual payments, or whose profile is blank — tap „…\" in the header and report.",
    "chatSafetyOpenCenter": "Open Safety Center",
    "chatSafetyHint": "You can come back here anytime — the page opens when no conversation is selected.",
    "chatQuizTitle": "Quick safety check",
    "chatQuizIntro": "Five situations that really happen in chat. Pick what you would do - you get the reasoning after each answer.",
    "chatQuizStart": "Start the quiz",
    "chatQuizProgress": "Question {current} of {total}",
    "chatQuizCorrect": "Correct",
    "chatQuizWrong": "Not quite",
    "chatQuizNext": "Next",
    "chatQuizSeeResult": "See result",
    "chatQuizScore": "{score} out of {total} correct",
    "chatQuizResultPerfect": "Flawless. That is exactly what a safe swap looks like.",
    "chatQuizResultGood": "Nicely done. Reread the explanations for the ones you missed.",
    "chatQuizResultPoor": "Worth a pass through the Safety Center before your next swap.",
    "chatQuizRestart": "Take it again",
    "chatQuizQ1": "Someone wants your book and promises to send the money “as soon as it arrives”. What do you do?",
    "chatQuizQ1A": "Ship the book first - no swap happens without trust.",
    "chatQuizQ1B": "Settle payment before shipping, use cash on delivery, or meet in person.",
    "chatQuizQ1C": "Give them my card details so they can send the money directly.",
    "chatQuizQ1Explain": "“I'll pay once I get it” is the most common scam on any swap platform. Payment upfront, cash on delivery or an in-person handover are the options where you don't end up without the book and without the money. You never need card details to RECEIVE money.",
    "chatQuizQ2": "You get a chat link to a page that looks like ShelfShare and asks for your email and password again, to “confirm the delivery”.",
    "chatQuizQ2A": "Sign in quickly so the delivery isn't lost.",
    "chatQuizQ2B": "Sign in, then change my password right after.",
    "chatQuizQ2C": "Don't open the link, don't type anything, and report the conversation.",
    "chatQuizQ2Explain": "ShelfShare never asks for your password through a link sent in chat. A page that does is a copy built to steal your account, and a password typed there is already gone - changed afterwards or not.",
    "chatQuizQ3": "A user asks for the verification code you received by email or SMS, “to confirm you're a real person”.",
    "chatQuizQ3A": "Never send it - that code opens my account, it confirms nothing about me.",
    "chatQuizQ3B": "Send it if their profile has good reviews.",
    "chatQuizQ3C": "Send it, but ask for their code too.",
    "chatQuizQ3Explain": "Verification codes are for you alone. Anyone asking for yours is trying to get into your account, or to confirm an action in your name that you never took.",
    "chatQuizQ4": "You've agreed on a swap and now you have to meet. Where do you suggest?",
    "chatQuizQ4A": "At my place - simplest option.",
    "chatQuizQ4B": "Somewhere public and busy, during the day, and I tell someone close to me where I'm going.",
    "chatQuizQ4C": "The parking lot behind the building, in the evening, so it's quiet.",
    "chatQuizQ4Explain": "A café, a bookshop or a busy station, in daylight, costs you nothing extra and changes everything if something is off. Your home address stays yours.",
    "chatQuizQ5": "Before anything is agreed, someone insists on moving the conversation to another app and asks for your full address.",
    "chatQuizQ5A": "Give both - otherwise it looks like I don't trust them.",
    "chatQuizQ5B": "Give the address only, not the number.",
    "chatQuizQ5C": "Stay in the app's chat until we agree; the address only if I choose home delivery.",
    "chatQuizQ5Explain": "A conversation inside the app can be reported and reviewed by the team; one moved elsewhere cannot. Pushing to leave the app before anything is agreed is itself a signal.",
